13 And he also rebelled against king Nebuchadnezzar, who[ had] made him swear by God: but he stiffened his neck, and hardened his heart against turning unto Jehovah, the God of Israel.
14 Moreover all the chiefs of the priests, and the people, tresp[assed very greatly] after all the abominations of the nations; and they polluted the house of Jehovah which he[ had hallowed] in Jerusalem.
16 but they mocked the messengers of God, and despised his words, and scoff[ed] at his prophets, until the wrath of Jehovah[ arose against his] people, till there[ was] no[ remedy].
